(default value is 5696). Note that server name is only a label, so it does not need to be the real host name of the server. key"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Although Gemalto SafeNet KeySecure uses an active-active clustered model; IBM Spectrum Virtualize asks for a primary server. The primary key server represents only the KeySecure server that is used for key create and rekey operations. Therefore; any of the clustered servers can be selected as the primary . key key","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":267.3819761204934,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":149.66666666666666,"r":546.3333333333334,"t":319.0},"charspan":[0,315],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/30","text":"Although Gemalto SafeNet KeySecure uses an active-active clustered model; IBM Spectrum Virtualize asks for a primary server. The primary key server represents only the KeySecure server that is used for key create and rekey operations. Therefore; any of the clustered servers can be selected as the primary . key key"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"Selecting a primary server is beneficial for load balancing. Any four servers can be used to retrieve the master key key key.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":238.04864278716002,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":150.0,"r":546.0,"t":264.66666666666663},"charspan":[0,125],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/31","text":"Selecting a primary server is beneficial for load balancing. Any four servers can be used to retrieve the master key key key."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"furniture","label":"page_footer","orig":"Chapter 12. Encryption 637","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":25.66666666666663,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":422.0,"r":548.0,"t":39.0},"charspan":[0,26],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/32","text":"Chapter 12. Encryption 637"}],"version":"1.10.0"}